        <mxCell id="n26" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n9" target="n17"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n27" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n9" target="n10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n28" value="no" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n10" target="n13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n29" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n10" target="n11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n30" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n11" target="n18"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n31" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n11" target="n12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n32" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n12" target="n15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n33" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n13" target="n14"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n34" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n15" target="n16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n35" value="days later" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;strokeColor=#c62828;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n18" target="n19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n36" value="THE HALF THAT DOES NOT EXIST: STATUS SYNC&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Zoldify calls GHN once, stores order_code, and never speaks to GHN again.&lt;br&gt;There is no webhook route and no polling job. Search the repository for a GHN&lt;br&gt;callback and there is nothing to find.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So picked up, in transit, delivered, delivery failed, returned to sender —&lt;br&gt;none of it reaches the order. `status` only moves when a human presses a&lt;br&gt;button in the seller UI.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;That matters more here than on an ordinary shop, because DELIVERED is the&lt;br&gt;event that releases the escrow. The money is waiting on a fact the system&lt;br&gt;cannot observe. Today a seller can mark their own order delivered and be paid&lt;br&gt;for a parcel that never left the house.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Two ways to close it: register a GHN webhook, or poll the tracking endpoint on&lt;br&gt;a schedule. The webhook is cheaper and faster; polling survives a missed call." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1080" width="800" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n37" value="Smaller things this diagram had to be honest about&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WEIGHT IS INVENTED. Every parcel is declared 500g, every line item 200g. GHN&lt;br&gt;prices by weight, so the quoted fee is fiction for anything heavier — and the&lt;br&gt;buyer already paid the quoted fee. Nothing in the product form asks for weight.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;THE FAILURE IS SWALLOWED ON PURPOSE, and that part is defensible: a shipment&lt;br&gt;is not money, and a seller can type the code in by hand. But it goes to&lt;br&gt;console.error, not the logger, so it lands nowhere anyone looks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;service_type_id = 2 IS HARDCODED. If a district only offers another service&lt;br&gt;type, the order simply gets no shipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;THE CARRIER IS ONE FIXED PICKUP POINT — GHN_FROM_DISTRICT_ID out of the&lt;br&gt;environment. Every parcel is declared as leaving the same address, no matter&lt;br&gt;which seller it belongs to. That is a warehouse model, and Zoldify is a&lt;br&gt;marketplace of individuals." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="1080" width="800" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
